-- The FTC disclosure item shipped, which matters out of proportion to its size:
-- it gated every affiliate link on the site, and affiliate is the primary
-- revenue line. in_test rather than in_production because two things still
-- stand between this and money — counsel review of the page, and actually
-- joining a programme. Neither is a code change.
--
-- Keep in sync with supabase/seed.sql (CI enforces this).

update public.roadmap_items
  set status = 'in_test',
      dev_percent_complete = 90,
      description = 'Shipped 2026-09-15, and it had to ship first because it gated every affiliate link on the site. THE STATE IT REPLACED: /calculators/battery linked source_url, the manufacturer spec citation, while retailer_url — the field scrape-signaturesolar.ts and scrape-a1solarstore.ts fill, and the only monetisable one — reached no visitor anywhere outside /admin/batteries. The primary revenue line was wired to nothing. THE FTC RULE is that a paid link carries a disclosure that is clear and conspicuous, near the link, before the click; a footer link is not enough. The way that rule breaks in practice is that the link and the disclosure are two separate edits and only one of them ships, so src/lib/affiliate.ts makes that shape impossible: `paid` is not a flag anyone remembers to set, it is true exactly when a programme template actually rewrote the URL, and the shelf disclosure, rel="sponsored" and the policy page all read that same boolean. A link cannot become paid without its disclosure appearing. TEMPLATES, NOT PARAMETERS: networks disagree on link shape — an in-house programme tends to append a parameter to the shop''s own URL, a network like Awin wraps it in a redirect on its own domain — and the shape is only knowable from the dashboard after a programme accepts you, so the repo holds the mechanism and NEXT_PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_* holds the shape. Committing a guessed ?ref= would be exactly the mistake the INVERTER_PRESETS admission gate exists to prevent. A template naming neither {URL} nor {URL_ENC} is refused rather than used, because an Awin link pasted without its ued tail is still a valid URL that still pays while sending every reader to one generic landing page — a failure that would never look broken from here. SHIPPED: src/lib/affiliate.ts (pure, 13 tests, no database or browser needed); components/AffiliateDisclosure.tsx, rendered above the shelf and only when something on it can actually earn; /affiliate-disclosure, built FROM the shop registry so it reports what is really configured rather than a hand-written claim that rots; a footer link; and Docker build args, because NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time and a tag set only in the server''s .env would be undefined in the browser and indistinguishable from "no programme yet". Spec-sheet citations are never tagged: a citation that quietly earned a commission is not a citation. FOUND ON THE WAY: SunGoldPower sells from its own site, so for those seven rows source_url IS the shop — the largest priced block in the catalogue, which a retailer_url-only rule would have left with no link at all. buyLink() therefore prefers retailer_url and falls back to a source_url that is itself a storefront, and collapses to one button when the shop page and the citation are the same page. NOT YET EARNING: no programme is signed up, so every template is unset, every link publishes clean and untagged, and no disclosure renders — which is the honest state, because nothing pays. Joining Signature Solar, SunGoldPower and A1 SolarStore is now the single remaining step between this and revenue, and it is not a code change. The page is still a draft rather than counsel-reviewed — see "Legal: professional review before production".'
  where title = 'Affiliate disclosure + FTC-compliant link policy';

-- This item has closed with "The FTC affiliate-disclosure item must still land
-- before any of these links go live" since 2026-08-26. It landed, so only that
-- closing sentence changes below; the rest of the description is re-stated
-- unchanged. Written as a literal rather than a replace() call on purpose —
-- check-roadmap-migrations.ts compares migrations to seed.sql statically, and a
-- function call is exactly the shape it cannot follow.
update public.roadmap_items
  set description = 'Affiliate is the primary revenue line, and the catalogue cannot currently carry it. All three EG4 models now have a price and a retailer, captured from Signature Solar (scripts/scrape-signaturesolar.ts, a hand-verified SKU-to-URL mapping — the storefront splits "Indoor" and "AllWeather" variants of the same capacity into separate products, so a naive title match would have picked the wrong one half the time). battery_models gained retailer and retailer_url columns rather than overwriting source_url, which stays the manufacturer spec citation. Vendor-mix widening has started: Bluetti turned out not to fit at all and was dropped from the plan, because its battery packs are ecosystem-locked to its own power stations rather than usable with any inverter (its own FAQ: the B300K "can only be charged by connecting to the AC500/AC300/AC200L/AC200MAX") — the same lock-in this project already refuses on the monitoring side. A1 SolarStore, a multi-brand reseller with its own affiliate program, added Discover Energy Systems as a new brand instead (scripts/scrape-a1solarstore.ts): a 5.12kWh 48V rack-mount model at $1,683.40. Discover Energy Systems sells through a dealer network with no storefront of its own, same as Victron — the row first cited A1 SolarStore''s product page for specs, which was caught as exactly the mistake source_url exists to prevent, so specs are now hardcoded from the manufacturer''s own datasheet (verified 51.2V, 100Ah, 5.12kWh, 100% usable DoD against A1 SolarStore''s numbers, which matched) and only price is scraped live from the retailer. All new and updated rows are unpublished pending admin review. Remaining: Victron stays editorial (no affiliate programme found); more of A1 SolarStore''s catalogue is worth a look (spotted but not yet verified: a Midnite Power 314Ah battery, and an EG4 "Indoor" 314Ah variant this catalogue is missing entirely) but its listings mix in bulk lead-acid pallets and bundled inverter+battery kits that do not belong here, so each addition needs the same manufacturer-datasheet verification as Discover Energy Systems. The FTC affiliate-disclosure item landed 2026-09-15, so the links are now live on /calculators/battery — publishing clean and untagged, because no affiliate programme has been joined yet. Joining one is what turns them into revenue, and it is the only remaining blocker that is not a code change.'
  where title = 'Battery catalogue: price coverage and vendor mix for affiliate';
